    },
    {
      "finding": "Free planning has mixed effects in Qwen: corrects recording and bottle replies but creates an invalid meeting acceptance.",
      "examples": [
        "COMP1-008",
        "COMP1-012",
        "COMP1-002"
      ]
    },
    {
      "finding": "Categorical Qwen prototype does not establish intent-conditioning gains. Incoming labels and reply acts are often inappropriate: invitation classified as status request with accept act; unedited video classified as invitation.",
      "examples": [
        "COMP1-001",
        "COMP1-010"
      ]
    },
    {
      "finding": "A factual constraint list can still yield an incorrect realization: Qwen meeting plan records departure and duration but renderer accepts incompatible start.",
      "examples": [
        "COMP1-002"
      ]
    },
    {
      "finding": "Correct standard replies can be corrupted by rewriting: Qwen turns $8 counterproposal into refusal of $8, reverses drink buyer, and adds unrelated meal suggestion to clinic well wishes.",
      "examples": [
        "COMP1-015",
        "COMP1-022",
        "COMP1-020"
      ]
    },
    {
      "finding": "mT5 oracle rewrites independently change negation, ownership and concrete details, so its rewrite failure is not only inherited from STANDARD.",
      "examples": [
        "COMP1-003",
        "COMP1-006",
        "COMP1-010",
        "COMP1-012"
      ]
    },
    {
      "finding": "Gemma planning is not error-free: its presentation plan assigns presenter facts to user while replying to peer relief. Good final reply does not validate the plan.",
      "examples": [
        "COMP1-017"
      ]
    },
    {
      "finding": "Unspecified meeting location remains unclarified by chat-model final replies; mT5 invents library.",
      "examples": [
        "COMP1-024"
      ]
    },
    {
      "finding": "Several emotional-dialogue contexts switch first-person speaker across turns (017-020); treat ownership ambiguity separately from clear timing, negation and colour contradictions.",
      "examples": [
        "COMP1-017",
        "COMP1-018",
        "COMP1-019",
        "COMP1-020"
      ]
    }
  ],
